nintendo's new president tatsumi  kimishima has vowed that the company  will continue to support the wii u  despite the consoles underperformance  and the fact that its successor the NX  could launch as early as next year in an  interview with time p Mishima  acknowledged the wii u's struggles but  said it's imperative that people who  bought the wii u feel supported and  satisfied when asked how long we you  would remain a core platform for  nintendo he said as you know within the  game business momentum is key when you  have momentum whether it's a platform or  software sales increase at this point in  the wii u lifespan we are looking at ten  million sell through for the hardware  itself which is just about a tenth of  what we sold overall for weed by  Nintendo's latest count the wii u had  sold 10.7 three million units by  comparison the original we crossed 100  million units sold more than two years  ago outpacing the xbox 360 and the ps3  kimishima went on to say nintendo has no  plans to abandon the wii u anytime soon  what I want to do what I think our first  job right now is to make sure that the  customers those ten million customers  who have a wii u at home have software  to play and we need to make sure that  they're satisfied with their purchase  and continue to enjoy playing on this  platform you can't just abandon them and  say hey it's time to move on to the next  thing upcoming wii u games from nintendo  include The Legend of Zelda Twilight  Princess HD Star Fox zero pokin  tournament and a brand new Legend of  Zelda game Nintendo does not plan to  talk in any official capacity about the  NX or whatever it ends up being called  until 2016 however kimishima has said  the platform will be dramatically  different than the wii u the NX was  first revealed in march 2015 on the same  day that nintendo announced plans to  make smartphone games the announcement  of the NX was purposefully made so  people would understand that nintendo  remains  to the console space then president  satoru iwata who passed away in July  refer to the NX as a brand new concept
 

